CommitDate: Wed Oct 14 16:48:41 2026 +0800

    [CI] Add requested file and directory downloads to nightly runs (#18368)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Add `--download` to PR-triggered and manually dispatched nightly runs so
    a requested file or directory can be downloaded as a GitHub Actions
    artifact. Accept absolute paths, paths relative to the test repository,
    and per-node mappings such as
    `[{"node0":"/path/a"},{"node1":"/path/b"}]`.
    
    Single-node jobs archive the requested path after the test. For
    multi-node jobs, CI archives requested paths once after the test
    finishes and before deleting the Pods. An exit trap and Kubernetes
    preStop hook cover Pods that exit earlier. Normal Pod deletion keeps the
    original grace period, so downloading small files does not add a fixed
    10-minute wait. Collection and upload errors do not change the test
    result. Common credential paths and files are excluded.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. `/nightly` and nightly workflow dispatch accept an optional
    `--download` request, and successful collections appear as downloadable
    workflow artifacts.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Parsed the modified workflow YAML.
    - Ran `bash -n` on `run.sh` and `download_archive.sh`.
    - Verified that archiving a directory does not include the output
    archive itself.
    - Ran `git diff --check`.
    - The Kubernetes Pod lifecycle and artifact upload still require CI
    validation; no NPU or Kubernetes environment was available locally.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
    ---------
    
    Signed-off-by: chenzeyu <2978509328@qq.com>

